#: src/nodejs-installation.md:1
msgid "Node.js Installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/nodejs-installation.md:3
msgid ""
"[just-install](https://npmjs.com/package/just-install) can be used to "
"automate installation of `just` in Node.js applications."
msgstr ""

#: src/nodejs-installation.md:6
msgid ""
"`just` is a great, more robust alternative to npm scripts. If you want to "
"include `just` in the dependencies of a Node.js application, `just-install` "
"will install a local, platform-specific binary as part of the `npm install` "
"command. This removes the need for every developer to install `just` "
"independently using one of the processes mentioned above. After "
"installation, the `just` command will work in npm scripts or with npx. It’s "
"great for teams who want to make the setup process for their project as easy "
"as possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/nodejs-installation.md:14
msgid ""
"For more information, see the [just-install README file](https://github.com/"
"brombal/just-install#readme)."
msgstr ""
